  "summary": {
    "en": "The junta has intensified attacks, bombing a religious ceremony and killing its own prisoners of war in Chin State, and launching an arson spree in Sagaing after a colonel was killed. Thailand has halted unofficial border trade for a week and border villagers in Tak province are seeking protection as artillery shells from Myanmar strike Thai homes. Japan is lobbying to have Myanmar removed from the global financial watchdog's blacklist while the United States is accused of undermining the EU's diplomatic blockade and seeking Myanmar's rare earths. The conflict caused 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
    "nb": "Juntaen har økt angrepene, bombet en religiøs seremoni og drept sine egne krigsfanger i Chin-staten, og startet en brannserie i Sagaing etter at en oberst ble drept. Thailand har stanset uoffisiell grensehandel i en uke, og grensebeboere i Tak-provinsen ber om beskyttelse etter at artillerigranater fra Myanmar traff thailandske hjem. Japan lobbyer for at Myanmar skal fjernes fra den globale finansielle tilsynsmyndighetens svarteliste, mens USA blir anklaget for å undergrave EUs diplomatiske blokade og søke etter Myanmars sjeldne jordarter. Konflikten forårsaket 2 332 dødsfall i kamp i 2024, ifølge UCDP.",
